        {
          "id": 1084574862,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> I suppose calling GINT_TO_POINTER on the value after dereferencing would work for storing it.\n\n`GUINT_TO_POINTER()`, as it's an unsigned integer, for cleanliness if nothing else.  (I don't know whether there will be any sign-extension issues on LP64/LLP64 platforms (on which most users are probably running these days), given that `GPOINTER_TO_{U}INT()` would cut off the bits into which the uppermost bit was sign-extended.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
